CAT = "phcleTrafficFireDrugs"; SEG = "TFD"
# Crime Detection and Investigation, part 2: traffic management and accident investigation,
# fire protection and arson investigation, vice and drug education and control.
Q = [
("The basic law on land transportation, driver's licenses and traffic rules in the Philippines is:",
 "R.A. 4136", ["R.A. 10586", "R.A. 8750", "P.D. 96"],
 "R.A. 4136, the Land Transportation and Traffic Code of 1964, governs vehicle registration, licensing and traffic rules. R.A. 10586 is the Anti-Drunk and Drugged Driving Act and R.A. 8750 the Seat Belts Use Act."),
("The law that makes wearing seat belts mandatory for drivers and front-seat passengers of motor vehicles is:",
 "R.A. 8750", ["R.A. 10054", "R.A. 10913", "R.A. 4136"],
 "R.A. 8750, the Seat Belts Use Act of 1999, requires seat belts for drivers and front-seat passengers of running vehicles, and for back-seat passengers of most private cars. R.A. 10054 is the Motorcycle Helmet Act and R.A. 10913 the Anti-Distracted Driving Act."),
("Under R.A. 11229, a child is not allowed in the front seat of a motor vehicle with a running engine if the child is:",
 "12 years old or younger", ["15 years old or younger", "7 years old or younger", "Under 18 years old"],
 "R.A. 11229 bars children 12 and below from the front seat, with an exception for a child who meets the height requirement for using the regular seat belt. Children must use a child restraint system unless exempted."),
("The five pillars of traffic management are traffic engineering, education, enforcement, environment and:",
 "Economy", ["Evaluation", "Emergency response", "Equipment"],
 "Traffic engineering, education, enforcement, environment and economy are the five pillars (the five E's) taught in traffic management. Enforcement alone cannot keep roads safe without the others."),
("In accident investigation, the event that turns a traffic situation into an accident, such as the first contact, is the:",
 "Key event", ["Point of possible perception", "Final position", "Start of evasive action"],
 "The key event characterizes the accident, usually the first harmful event such as the first collision. Perception, reaction and evasive action come before it in the chain of events."),
("The doctrine that the party who had the last opportunity to avoid an accident, and failed to, is liable is the:",
 "Last clear chance", ["State of necessity", "Res ipsa loquitur", "Proximate cause"],
 "Last clear chance holds liable the person who had the final opportunity to prevent the harm. Res ipsa loquitur infers negligence from the nature of an accident."),
("The fire tetrahedron adds which element to fuel, heat and oxygen?",
 "Uninhibited chemical chain reaction", ["A source of ignition", "Smoke and toxic gases", "Moisture in the fuel load"],
 "The tetrahedron adds the self-sustaining chemical chain reaction, which is why some extinguishing agents work by interrupting it rather than by cooling or smothering."),
("Under Article 320 of the Revised Penal Code, as amended by R.A. 7659, burning a train, ship or building used for public gatherings is:",
 "Destructive arson", ["Simple arson", "Malicious mischief", "Reckless imprudence"],
 "Article 320 lists the property whose burning is destructive arson, including public buildings, places of assembly and means of transport. Other arson is governed by P.D. 1613."),
("In fire investigation, the V-shaped burn pattern on a wall generally points down toward the:",
 "Point of origin", ["Area of heaviest smoke", "Last area to burn", "Exit of the hot gases"],
 "Fire burns upward and outward, so the bottom of the V usually marks where the fire began. The investigator confirms it with other indicators before concluding."),
("Charred wood showing a checkered pattern of cracks, studied by fire investigators, is called:",
 "Alligatoring", ["Spalling", "Crazing", "Annealing"],
 "Alligatoring is the blistered, checkered char on burned wood. Spalling is the breaking away of concrete or masonry under heat; crazing is the fine cracking of glass."),
("The Fire Code of the Philippines of 2008 is:",
 "R.A. 9514", ["R.A. 9263", "P.D. 1613", "P.D. 1185"],
 "R.A. 9514 is the Revised Fire Code of 2008, which replaced P.D. 1185. P.D. 1613 is the law on arson, and R.A. 9263 professionalized the BFP and BJMP."),
("In arson investigation, more than one separate point of origin in a fire usually indicates:",
 "A deliberately set fire", ["An electrical short circuit", "A fire started by lightning", "Spontaneous heating"],
 "Multiple unconnected points of origin are a classic sign of an incendiary fire. Accidental fires usually start at a single point."),
("Materials such as gasoline-soaked rags used to spread a fire from one area to another are called:",
 "Trailers", ["Plants", "Accelerant residue", "Alligatoring"],
 "Trailers carry the fire along a path. Plants are the materials placed to start the fire; alligatoring is the checked pattern of charred wood."),
("The lead agency in the enforcement of R.A. 9165, the Comprehensive Dangerous Drugs Act of 2002, is the:",
 "Philippine Drug Enforcement Agency", ["Dangerous Drugs Board", "National Bureau of Investigation", "Department of Health"],
 "R.A. 9165 made PDEA the implementing arm and lead anti-drug law enforcement agency. The Dangerous Drugs Board is the policy-making and strategy-formulating body."),
("Under Section 21 of R.A. 9165, as amended by R.A. 10640, seized drugs must be inventoried and photographed in the presence of the accused, an elected public official and a representative of:",
 "The prosecution service or the media", ["The barangay tanod on duty in the area", "The Commission on Human Rights", "The Public Attorney's Office"],
 "R.A. 10640 reduced the required witnesses to an elected public official and a representative of the National Prosecution Service or the media, besides the accused or his counsel. This protects the chain of custody."),
("An operation in which an officer poses as a buyer of illegal drugs to catch the seller in the act is a:",
 "Buy-bust operation", ["Controlled delivery", "Instigation", "Search and seizure"],
 "A buy-bust is a form of entrapment, which is lawful. Instigation, where officers induce a person to commit a crime he had no intent to commit, is an absolutory cause."),
("Methamphetamine hydrochloride, known locally as shabu, is classified as a:",
 "Stimulant", ["Depressant", "Hallucinogen", "Narcotic analgesic"],
 "Shabu stimulates the central nervous system, raising alertness and heart rate. Depressants such as sedatives slow it; hallucinogens such as LSD distort perception."),
("Marijuana comes from the plant:",
 "Cannabis sativa", ["Papaver somniferum", "Erythroxylum coca", "Ephedra sinica"],
 "Marijuana is from Cannabis sativa. Opium comes from Papaver somniferum, cocaine from Erythroxylum coca, and ephedrine, a precursor of shabu, from Ephedra."),
("Dark marks left on the pavement by tires that are locked and sliding without rotating are:",
 "Skid marks", ["Yaw marks", "Scuff marks", "Gouge marks"],
 "Skid marks come from locked wheels and help estimate speed and the point of braking. Yaw marks are curved marks from tires sliding sideways while still rotating; gouges are cut by metal parts."),
("Prostitution, gambling and drunkenness are classed in police work as:",
 "Vices", ["Index crimes", "Cybercrimes", "Felonies against persons"],
 "Vices are habits or practices considered immoral or harmful, covered in vice control. Index crimes are serious crimes against persons and property used to measure the crime rate."),
]
